+## Troubleshooting
 
-## Documentation
+**`yarn fork` is slow, or the app shows RPC errors.** The public `https://mainnet.base.org` endpoint rate
+limits, and a fork fetches state lazily on every miss. Point `FORK_URL` at your own RPC and pin `FORK_BLOCK`.
 
-Visit our [docs](https://docs.scaffoldeth.io) to learn how to start building with Scaffold-ETH 2.
+**`anvil_dealERC20` fails.** Your Foundry predates the cheat RPC. Run `foundryup`.
 
-To know more about its features, check out our [website](https://scaffoldeth.io).
+**The feed is empty after restarting anvil.** Expected — the fork's state is in memory. Re-run `yarn deploy`
+and `yarn fund`.
 
-## Contributing to Scaffold-ETH 2
+**`localStorage.getItem is not a function` when running Next directly.** Node 22.4+ exposes a `localStorage`
+global with no methods on it, and RainbowKit feature-detects Web Storage before calling it. `yarn start`,
+`yarn next:build` and `yarn ipfs:build` all go through `packages/nextjs/scripts/run-next.mjs`, which adds
+`--no-experimental-webstorage` on the Node versions that need it. Running `npx next dev` directly bypasses
+that wrapper.
 
